  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is added and exported, and `python -m pytest tests/test_types.py -q` passes (48 passed, 2 skipped).\n\n- **Implementation:** `KeyValue` is a `ParamType` subclass in `src/click/types.py`, right after `UUIDParameterType`, with `name = \"key_value\"`. It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- **Errors:** input with no `=` or with an empty key calls `self.fail(...)` with `'<value>' is not a valid key=value pair.`.\n- **Export:** the class itself is exported from `src/click/__init__.py`, so `type=click.KeyValue()` works as in your example.\n- **Tests:** `tests/test_types.py` has a parametrized valid-input test and an invalid-input test (`novalue`, `=value`, empty string).\n\nI also made `convert()` return an existing tuple unchanged, so defaults already given as `(key, value)` pass through.",
